    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Разбудил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did I wake you?' You'll hear 'to wake up' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to wake up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Прости меня, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please forgive me.' Max puts 'sorry' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'me'. Vika answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ты вообще был?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where were you, anyway?' You'll hear 'where' all the time in the show, here connected with 'was'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что тут допрос такой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What is this, an interrogation?' Notice the word order: 'what' comes first, and 'interrogation' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты считаешь, что можешь шляться где угодно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You think you can wander off anywhere?' The reflexive ending on the verb for 'wander' turns the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И приходить в три часа?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And stroll in at three o'clock?' Vika starts with 'to come' and pairs it with 'three' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Без пятнадцати.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quarter to.' Max puts 'fifteen' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'fifteen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что у нас за отношения?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of relationship do we have?' The key word here means 'what', which Vika combines with 'us'. And Max jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "У нас свободные отношения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have an open relationship.' The key word here means 'us', which Max combines with 'free'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Все хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything is fine.' A compact expression built around 'good' and 'good'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Раз у нас свободные отношения,",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Since we have an open relationship,' A compact expression built around 'time' and 'relations'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "На сегодня ты свободен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are free for tonight.' Here 'today' sets up the idea, while 'free' comes at the end for emphasis.",
